{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"proposal-source-companion-packages-for-ai-code-exploration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Proposal: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-source"},{"type":"text","value":" Companion Packages for AI Code Exploration"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"problem","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AI agents (Claude, Cursor, Copilot, etc.) work best when they can grep and read actual source code. Our npm packages only contain built output (transpiled JS, type definitions), not the original TypeScript source."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current workarounds:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clone repos to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/tmp"},{"type":"text","value":" manually"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ask the agent to clone and explore"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read minified/transpiled code (poor results)"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These are clunky and break the flow of AI-assisted development."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"proposal","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Proposal"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Publish companion "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-source"},{"type":"text","value":" packages alongside every TanStack library release:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"# Normal install (built output, what runs in production)\nnpm install @tanstack/react-query@5.62.0\n\n# Source install for AI exploration (dev only)\nnpm install @tanstack/react-query-source@5.62.0 --save-dev","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-source"},{"type":"text","value":" package contains the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/"},{"type":"text","value":" directory from the monorepo package (TypeScript and JavaScript source). It's not meant to be imported at runtime, only explored by AI agents."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"structure","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structure"}]},{"type":"code","value":"node_modules/@tanstack/react-query-source/\n  src/\n    useQuery.ts\n    useMutation.ts\n    QueryClient.ts\n    ...\n  package.json"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"mcp-integration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MCP Integration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hosted MCP server gets a simple tool:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"get_source_instructions({ library: 'query' })","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  \"package\": \"@tanstack/react-query-source\",\n  \"install\": \"npm install @tanstack/react-query-source@5.62.0 --save-dev\",\n  \"explorePath\": \"node_modules/@tanstack/react-query-source/src/\",\n  \"note\": \"Install this package to explore TanStack Query source code. Use your file tools to grep and read.\"\n}","lang":"json"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The agent installs the package, then uses its native file system tools (grep, read) to explore. No custom MCP tooling for search/read needed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"implementation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Implementation"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"1-ci-cd-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. CI/CD Changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On every release, publish two packages:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"# Pseudocode\n- name: Publish main package\n  run: npm publish\n\n- name: Publish source package\n  run: |\n    # Create temp package with only src/\n    cp -r src/ dist-source/src/\n    cp package.json dist-source/\n    # Modify package name to add -source suffix\n    jq '.name += \"-source\"' dist-source/package.json > tmp && mv tmp dist-source/package.json\n    # Modify files field to only include src/\n    jq '.files = [\"src\"]' dist-source/package.json > tmp && mv tmp dist-source/package.json\n    cd dist-source && npm publish","lang":"yaml"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"2-mcp-server-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. MCP Server Changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add one tool to the hosted MCP:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get_source_instructions"},{"type":"text","value":" - Returns install command and explore path for a library"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"3-documentation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Documentation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Update MCP docs to explain the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-source"},{"type":"text","value":" package convention."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"benefits","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Benefits"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No local CLI needed"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Hosted MCP only, agents handle the rest"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Standard npm workflow"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - No new tooling for developers to learn"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Version alignment"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Source version always matches installed version"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Works with any AI agent"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Just needs file system access"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Minimal overhead"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Source packages are small (just source files)"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tradeoffs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tradeoffs"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Double publish"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Every release publishes 2 packages per library"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"npm registry usage"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - More packages, though source packages are small"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agent must run npm install"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - One extra step, but agents already know how"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"alternatives-considered","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alternatives Considered"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"local-cli-that-caches-repos","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Local CLI that caches repos"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rejected: Adds complexity, requires users to install a CLI, duplicates what npm already does."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hosted-grep-api-sourcegraph-backed","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hosted grep API (Sourcegraph-backed)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rejected: External dependency, rate limits, adds context overhead for every query."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"include-source-in-main-package","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Include source in main package"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rejected: Bloats production installs, source isn't needed at runtime."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"github-raw-content-proxy-via-mcp","children":[{"type":"text","value":"GitHub raw content proxy via MCP"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rejected: Can't grep across files, need to know exact paths upfront."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"open-questions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open Questions"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Should we include related packages? (e.g., "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/query-core"},{"type":"text","value":" source in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-query-source"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What about monorepo-level files like shared utilities?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Should we include tests in the source package?"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prototype the publish workflow for one library (react-query)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Test with Claude/Cursor to validate the agent experience"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Roll out to all TanStack libraries"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add MCP tool and documentation"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"proposal-source-companion-packages-for-ai-code-exploration","text":"Proposal: -source Companion Packages for AI Code Exploration","level":1},{"id":"problem","text":"Problem","level":2},{"id":"proposal","text":"Proposal","level":2},{"id":"structure","text":"Structure","level":2},{"id":"mcp-integration","text":"MCP Integration","level":2},{"id":"implementation","text":"Implementation","level":2},{"id":"1-ci-cd-changes","text":"1. CI/CD Changes","level":3},{"id":"2-mcp-server-changes","text":"2. MCP Server Changes","level":3},{"id":"3-documentation","text":"3. Documentation","level":3},{"id":"benefits","text":"Benefits","level":2},{"id":"tradeoffs","text":"Tradeoffs","level":2},{"id":"alternatives-considered","text":"Alternatives Considered","level":2},{"id":"local-cli-that-caches-repos","text":"Local CLI that caches repos","level":3},{"id":"hosted-grep-api-sourcegraph-backed","text":"Hosted grep API (Sourcegraph-backed)","level":3},{"id":"include-source-in-main-package","text":"Include source in main package","level":3},{"id":"github-raw-content-proxy-via-mcp","text":"GitHub raw content proxy via MCP","level":3},{"id":"open-questions","text":"Open Questions","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# Proposal: `-source` Companion Packages for AI Code Exploration\n\n## Problem\n\nAI agents (Claude, Cursor, Copilot, etc.) work best when they can grep and read actual source code. Our npm packages only contain built output (transpiled JS, type definitions), not the original TypeScript source.\n\nCurrent workarounds:\n\n- Clone repos to `/tmp` manually\n- Ask the agent to clone and explore\n- Read minified/transpiled code (poor results)\n\nThese are clunky and break the flow of AI-assisted development.\n\n## Proposal\n\nPublish companion `-source` packages alongside every TanStack library release:\n\n```bash\n# Normal install (built output, what runs in production)\nnpm install @tanstack/react-query@5.62.0\n\n# Source install for AI exploration (dev only)\nnpm install @tanstack/react-query-source@5.62.0 --save-dev\n```\n\nThe `-source` package contains the `src/` directory from the monorepo package (TypeScript and JavaScript source). It's not meant to be imported at runtime, only explored by AI agents.\n\n## Structure\n\n```\nnode_modules/@tanstack/react-query-source/\n  src/\n    useQuery.ts\n    useMutation.ts\n    QueryClient.ts\n    ...\n  package.json\n```\n\n## MCP Integration\n\nThe hosted MCP server gets a simple tool:\n\n```typescript\nget_source_instructions({ library: 'query' })\n```\n\nReturns:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"package\": \"@tanstack/react-query-source\",\n  \"install\": \"npm install @tanstack/react-query-source@5.62.0 --save-dev\",\n  \"explorePath\": \"node_modules/@tanstack/react-query-source/src/\",\n  \"note\": \"Install this package to explore TanStack Query source code. Use your file tools to grep and read.\"\n}\n```\n\nThe agent installs the package, then uses its native file system tools (grep, read) to explore. No custom MCP tooling for search/read needed.\n\n## Implementation\n\n### 1. CI/CD Changes\n\nOn every release, publish two packages:\n\n```yaml\n# Pseudocode\n- name: Publish main package\n  run: npm publish\n\n- name: Publish source package\n  run: |\n    # Create temp package with only src/\n    cp -r src/ dist-source/src/\n    cp package.json dist-source/\n    # Modify package name to add -source suffix\n    jq '.name += \"-source\"' dist-source/package.json > tmp && mv tmp dist-source/package.json\n    # Modify files field to only include src/\n    jq '.files = [\"src\"]' dist-source/package.json > tmp && mv tmp dist-source/package.json\n    cd dist-source && npm publish\n```\n\n### 2. MCP Server Changes\n\nAdd one tool to the hosted MCP:\n\n- `get_source_instructions` - Returns install command and explore path for a library\n\n### 3. Documentation\n\nUpdate MCP docs to explain the `-source` package convention.\n\n## Benefits\n\n1. **No local CLI needed** - Hosted MCP only, agents handle the rest\n2. **Standard npm workflow** - No new tooling for developers to learn\n3. **Version alignment** - Source version always matches installed version\n4. **Works with any AI agent** - Just needs file system access\n5. **Minimal overhead** - Source packages are small (just source files)\n\n## Tradeoffs\n\n1. **Double publish** - Every release publishes 2 packages per library\n2. **npm registry usage** - More packages, though source packages are small\n3. **Agent must run npm install** - One extra step, but agents already know how\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n### Local CLI that caches repos\n\nRejected: Adds complexity, requires users to install a CLI, duplicates what npm already does.\n\n### Hosted grep API (Sourcegraph-backed)\n\nRejected: External dependency, rate limits, adds context overhead for every query.\n\n### Include source in main package\n\nRejected: Bloats production installs, source isn't needed at runtime.\n\n### GitHub raw content proxy via MCP\n\nRejected: Can't grep across files, need to know exact paths upfront.\n\n## Open Questions\n\n1. Should we include related packages? (e.g., `@tanstack/query-core` source in `@tanstack/react-query-source`)\n2. What about monorepo-level files like shared utilities?\n3. Should we include tests in the source package?\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. Prototype the publish workflow for one library (react-query)\n2. Test with Claude/Cursor to validate the agent experience\n3. Roll out to all TanStack libraries\n4. Add MCP tool and documentation\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# Proposal: `-source` Companion Packages for AI Code Exploration\n\n## Problem\n\nAI agents (Claude, Cursor, Copilot, etc.) work best when they can grep and read actual source code. Our npm packages only contain built output (transpiled JS, type definitions), not the original TypeScript source.\n\nCurrent workarounds:\n\n- Clone repos to `/tmp` manually\n- Ask the agent to clone and explore\n- Read minified/transpiled code (poor results)\n\nThese are clunky and break the flow of AI-assisted development.\n\n## Proposal\n\nPublish companion `-source` packages alongside every TanStack library release:\n\n```bash\n# Normal install (built output, what runs in production)\nnpm install @tanstack/react-query@5.62.0\n\n# Source install for AI exploration (dev only)\nnpm install @tanstack/react-query-source@5.62.0 --save-dev\n```\n\nThe `-source` package contains the `src/` directory from the monorepo package (TypeScript and JavaScript source). It's not meant to be imported at runtime, only explored by AI agents.\n\n## Structure\n\n```\nnode_modules/@tanstack/react-query-source/\n  src/\n    useQuery.ts\n    useMutation.ts\n    QueryClient.ts\n    ...\n  package.json\n```\n\n## MCP Integration\n\nThe hosted MCP server gets a simple tool:\n\n```typescript\nget_source_instructions({ library: 'query' })\n```\n\nReturns:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"package\": \"@tanstack/react-query-source\",\n  \"install\": \"npm install @tanstack/react-query-source@5.62.0 --save-dev\",\n  \"explorePath\": \"node_modules/@tanstack/react-query-source/src/\",\n  \"note\": \"Install this package to explore TanStack Query source code. Use your file tools to grep and read.\"\n}\n```\n\nThe agent installs the package, then uses its native file system tools (grep, read) to explore. No custom MCP tooling for search/read needed.\n\n## Implementation\n\n### 1. CI/CD Changes\n\nOn every release, publish two packages:\n\n```yaml\n# Pseudocode\n- name: Publish main package\n  run: npm publish\n\n- name: Publish source package\n  run: |\n    # Create temp package with only src/\n    cp -r src/ dist-source/src/\n    cp package.json dist-source/\n    # Modify package name to add -source suffix\n    jq '.name += \"-source\"' dist-source/package.json > tmp && mv tmp dist-source/package.json\n    # Modify files field to only include src/\n    jq '.files = [\"src\"]' dist-source/package.json > tmp && mv tmp dist-source/package.json\n    cd dist-source && npm publish\n```\n\n### 2. MCP Server Changes\n\nAdd one tool to the hosted MCP:\n\n- `get_source_instructions` - Returns install command and explore path for a library\n\n### 3. Documentation\n\nUpdate MCP docs to explain the `-source` package convention.\n\n## Benefits\n\n1. **No local CLI needed** - Hosted MCP only, agents handle the rest\n2. **Standard npm workflow** - No new tooling for developers to learn\n3. **Version alignment** - Source version always matches installed version\n4. **Works with any AI agent** - Just needs file system access\n5. **Minimal overhead** - Source packages are small (just source files)\n\n## Tradeoffs\n\n1. **Double publish** - Every release publishes 2 packages per library\n2. **npm registry usage** - More packages, though source packages are small\n3. **Agent must run npm install** - One extra step, but agents already know how\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n### Local CLI that caches repos\n\nRejected: Adds complexity, requires users to install a CLI, duplicates what npm already does.\n\n### Hosted grep API (Sourcegraph-backed)\n\nRejected: External dependency, rate limits, adds context overhead for every query.\n\n### Include source in main package\n\nRejected: Bloats production installs, source isn't needed at runtime.\n\n### GitHub raw content proxy via MCP\n\nRejected: Can't grep across files, need to know exact paths upfront.\n\n## Open Questions\n\n1. Should we include related packages? (e.g., `@tanstack/query-core` source in `@tanstack/react-query-source`)\n2. What about monorepo-level files like shared utilities?\n3. Should we include tests in the source package?\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. Prototype the publish workflow for one library (react-query)\n2. Test with Claude/Cursor to validate the agent experience\n3. Roll out to all TanStack libraries\n4. Add MCP tool and documentation\n"}
